$$$Ps.3.1
<title type="psalm" canonical="true">A Psalm of David, when he fled from Absalom his son.</title><divineName>LORD</divineName>, how are they increased that trouble me! many <transChange type="added">are</transChange> they that rise up against me.
$$$Ps.3.2
Many <transChange type="added">there be</transChange> which say of my soul, <q marker="">There is no help for him in God.</q> <seg type="x-selah">Selah.</seg>
$$$Ps.4.0
<title type="psalm" canonical="true">To the chief Musician on Neginoth, A Psalm of David.</title>
$$$Ps.4.1
<l level="1">Hear me when I call, O God of my righteousness:</l><l level="2">thou hast enlarged me <transChange type="added">when I was</transChange> in distress;</l><l level="2">have mercy upon me, and hear my prayer.</l>
$$$John.3.16
<title type="section" subType="x-preverse">God’s love for the world</title><q who="Jesus" marker="" sID="q1"/><w lemma="strong:G1063" morph="robinson:CONJ">For</w> <w lemma="strong:G2316" morph="robinson:N-NSM">God</w> <w lemma="strong:G3779" morph="robinson:ADV">so</w> <w lemma="strong:G25" morph="robinson:V-AAI-3S">loved</w> <w lemma="strong:G3588 strong:G2889" morph="robinson:T-ASM robinson:N-ASM">the world</w>, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.<note type="crossReference" osisRef="John.3.16" n="a"><reference osisRef="Rom.5.8">Rom. 5:8</reference>; <reference osisRef="1John.4.9">1 John 4:9</reference></note>
$$$John.3.17
For God sent not his Son into the world to condemn the world; but that the world through him might be saved.<note type="study" n="b">Or, <catchWord>condemn</catchWord>: judge.</note><q eID="q1" marker=""/><figure src="map.png"/>
